---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";

const basePath = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Troubleshooting"
  description="Fix common Veasel Code install, connect, sandbox, and session issues."
>
  <section class="doc-page">
    <p class="kicker">FIELD GUIDE / TROUBLESHOOTING</p>
    <h1>
      When something
      <br />
      <em>stalls.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Short checks for the paths people hit first. For deeper contracts, open
      the linked runtime docs.
    </p>

    <div class="doc-panel faq-panel">
      <h2>veasel cannot find a server / health fails</h2>
      <p>
        Default listen address is <code>127.0.0.1:4097</code>. Run{" "}
        <code>veasel serve</code> alone if another client needs the API. Only
        unauthenticated loopback HTTP is accepted for{" "}
        <code>VEASEL_API_URL</code>. Non-loopback <code>Host</code> and browser{" "}
        <code>Origin</code> values are rejected.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel faq-panel">
      <h2>/connect or model discovery fails</h2>
      <p>
        Confirm the endpoint is HTTPS (or loopback HTTP for local servers).
        Placeholders such as a Cloudflare account ID must be replaced (Ctrl+U in
        full settings). A newly typed key is sent to the local server only for
        discovery and is saved when you choose a model. Environment variables
        are optional; a saved profile key wins for that provider.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel faq-panel">
      <h2>Shell review says no sandbox / unexpected wrap</h2>
      <p>
        Approval is always required. Platform sandboxes are defense-in-depth:
      </p>
      <ul class="guide-list">
        <li>
          Linux: Bubblewrap when <code>bwrap</code> is on <code>PATH</code>
        </li>
        <li>
          macOS: Seatbelt via <code>/usr/bin/sandbox-exec</code>
        </li>
        <li>Windows: AppContainer + Job Object when wrap can be created</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The default is <code>require</code>: a missing backend fails closed.
        Explicit <code>VEASEL_SHELL_SANDBOX=auto</code> permits unsandboxed
        fallback and does not advertise that capability. <code>off</code> never
        wraps. Network is denied unless{" "}
        <code>VEASEL_SHELL_SANDBOX_NETWORK=allow</code>. See{" "}
        <a href={`${basePath}/docs/security/`}>security</a> and{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/veasel-labs/veasel/blob/main/docs/SHELL_COMMANDS.md">
          SHELL_COMMANDS.md
        </a>
        .
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel faq-panel">
      <h2>Turn stuck as uncertain</h2>
      <p>
        After a crash during claimed work, Veasel marks the operation{" "}
        <code>uncertain</code> and never auto-retries. Inspect the workspace and
        operation status before sending another prompt.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel faq-panel">
      <h2>Skills or MCP missing</h2>
      <p>
        Confirm skill folders sit under a discovered root or{" "}
        <code>VEASEL_SKILLS_DIRS</code>. MCP needs per-session trust before tool
        calls can be approved. Skill scripts are never auto-run.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doc-panel faq-panel">
      <h2>Where to ask for help</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="https://github.com/veasel-labs/veasel/discussions">
          Discussions
        </a>
        ·{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/veasel-labs/veasel/blob/main/SUPPORT.md">
          SUPPORT.md
        </a>
        · private security reports via{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/veasel-labs/veasel/blob/main/SECURITY.md">
          SECURITY.md
        </a>
        .
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="doc-next">
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/faq/`}>
        FAQ <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/`}>
        Docs overview <span aria-hidden="true">↑</span>
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
